    "52c8330c-7f15-5091-b102-671604cbf174": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "2. Abbreviations used in this story",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 1.97,
        "extent": [
          -18924313.43,
          -7967317.54,
          21150703.25,
          14368684.28
        ],
        "enableIdentify": false,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "markdown": "*Glossary*\n\n| Abbr. | Full name | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **AQI** | Air Quality Index | 0–500 scale with six CPCB categories from Good to Severe |\n| **CPCB** | Central Pollution Control Board | India's national pollution regulator; runs the national AQI and monitoring network |\n| **GRAP** | Graded Response Action Plan | Pre-agreed measures by AQI band (Stages I–IV: construction limits, vehicle restrictions, online classes, work-from-home) |\n| **CAQM** | Commission for Air Quality Management in NCR and Adjoining Areas | The statutory body for air quality in Delhi-NCR; it invokes GRAP stages |\n| **DPCC** | Delhi Pollution Control Committee | Delhi government's pollution agency; operates the city's monitoring stations |\n| **NCR** | National Capital Region | Delhi plus neighbouring cities in Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Rajasthan (Gurugram, Noida and others) |\n| **NCT** | National Capital Territory of Delhi | Delhi's administrative territory; the bold outline on the map |\n| **PM2.5** | particulate matter smaller than 2.5 micrometres | Particles up to 2.5 µm across, in µg/m³ |\n| **PM10** | particulate matter smaller than 10 micrometres | Particles up to 10 µm across, in µg/m³ |\n| **CAMS** | Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service | The EU's global atmospheric-composition analysis and forecast service; input to the Air Pollution model |\n| **ERA5** | ECMWF Reanalysis, 5th generation | A gridded reconstruction of past weather; the Aurora 1.5 input in this example |\n| **IFS HRES T0** | Integrated Forecasting System, high resolution, analysis at lead time 0 | The real-time input Aurora 1.5 was fine-tuned on |\n| **IST** | Indian Standard Time | UTC+5:30 |\n| **BLH** | boundary-layer height | Depth of the lower atmosphere in which pollution mixes; lower means higher surface concentrations |\n",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": ""
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 2.0
        },
        "layerOverride": [
          {
            "targetLayer": "AQI 5 Nov 18:30 IST",
            "visible": false
          },
