        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "*5 · Output · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account) · Weather: Aurora 1.5 · Additional method*\n\nIn this run mixing height, wind and temperature come from Aurora 1.5 initialised with ARCO-ERA5; pollutant concentrations are synthetic (CAMS needs an account). The AQI values are therefore illustrative, while the stagnation hours are real model output.\n\n| Site | Now | Peak | Category | Dominant | GRAP | Stagnant h |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Anand Vihar | 385 | 500 | Severe | PM10 | 4 | 12 |\n| Dwarka Sector 8 | 336 | 406 | Severe | PM2.5 | 3 | 16 |\n| Gurugram Vikas Sadan | 376 | 479 | Severe | PM10 | 4 | 15 |\n| ITO | 383 | 498 | Severe | PM10 | 4 | 13 |\n| Jahangirpuri | 365 | 452 | Severe | PM10 | 4 | 14 |\n| Noida Sector 62 | 340 | 409 | Severe | PM2.5 | 3 | 10 |\n| Okhla Phase 2 | 366 | 453 | Severe | PM10 | 4 | 11 |\n| Punjabi Bagh | 346 | 415 | Severe | PM2.5 | 3 | 14 |\n| R K Puram | 335 | 405 | Severe | PM2.5 | 3 | 13 |\n| Rohini | 337 | 406 | Severe | PM2.5 | 3 | 16 |\n\nAll sites peak around 7 Nov 05:30 IST (minimum mixing height 64–75 m). Site colours on the map are the peak category; use ⓘ to click sites and cells for values. Output files: `pollutants_12h.csv`, `meteorology_hourly.csv`, `fused_hourly.csv`, `summary_by_site.csv`, `messages_{ko,en,hi}.json`, `bulletin_*.md`, `frontend/*.json`.\n",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": ""
        },
