    "cbe121fe-e65d-5426-b726-de7e93c78357": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "13. The truth about resolution",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 10.46,
        "extent": [
          8532638.97,
          3274212.69,
          8643958.46,
          3382011.46
        ],
        "enableIdentify": true,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "map",
          "markdown": "*6 · Limits and responsible use · Pollutants: synthetic (CAMS needs an account)*\n\nThe large square on the map is one 0.4° cell of the Air Pollution model. All of Delhi NCT fits in two or three cells.\n\n- **Spatial resolution**: site differences are interpolation, not roadside values. A real service needs per-station bias correction or fine-tuning on CPCB data.\n- **Temporal resolution**: the hourly curve is a linear interpolation of 12-hour forecasts; the hourly structure comes from 1.5's meteorology and the messages say so.\n- **Input data**: 1.5 was fine-tuned on IFS HRES T0; this example uses ERA5. The Air Pollution model is for CAMS analysis only.\n- **Gases at 1000 hPa**: NO2/SO2/O3/CO are converted mixing ratios, an approximation; PM2.5/PM10 dominate the AQI.\n- **Operational decisions**: Aurora is a research model and must not drive operational decisions without expert review.\n",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": ""
        },
        "transition": {
          "type": "smooth",
          "time": 2.0
        },
