    "b564f209-1f69-5393-8d4e-0227389eb8a1": {
      "type": "StorySegmentLayer",
      "name": "19. Done and still to do",
      "visible": true,
      "parameters": {
        "zoom": 7.65,
        "extent": [
          8293302.06,
          3061141.04,
          9072538.5,
          3829123.84
        ],
        "enableIdentify": false,
        "content": {
          "contentMode": "markdown",
          "markdown": "*7 · What remains · run it*\n\nThe five roadmap items were run in the scenes above. What remains: connecting real CPCB observations, the actual fine-tuning on regional data, and attaching a CAMS account so pollutant concentrations also come from Aurora.\n\n1. **Uncertainty**: `AuroraV1p5Ensemble` with `rollout_ensemble` for \"80% chance of stagnation\".\n2. **CPCB correction**: learn per-site residuals (linear or quantile mapping first).\n3. **Fine-tuning**: adapt the Air Pollution model to regional data with the loop in `msresearch-aurora/starter-code/`; model-side requirements in `docs/finetuning.md`.\n4. **Channels**: push `messages_hi.json` to the WhatsApp Business API, SMS or the Delhi government app; map users to the nearest site by pin code.\n5. **Automation**: cron `delhi_aq.py --mode foundry --plot` at 00 and 12 UTC.\n\n### Run it yourself\n\nDemo mode needs no GPU or data.\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora.git && cd aurora\npip install -e . && pip install matplotlib\npython examples/delhi_air_quality/delhi_aq.py --mode demo --date 2025-11-05 --plot --out outputs\n```\n\n- Notebook: [Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/github/playground-for-thinker/aurora/blob/main/examples/delhi_air_quality/example_delhi_air_quality.ipynb) · [Binder](https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/playground-for-thinker/aurora/main?labpath=examples%2Fdelhi_air_quality%2Fexample_delhi_air_quality.ipynb)\n- Storyboard (scene-by-scene document): [STORYBOARD.md](https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora/blob/main/examples/delhi_air_quality/STORYBOARD.md) · [STORYBOARD_kor.md](https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora/blob/main/examples/delhi_air_quality/STORYBOARD_kor.md)\n- Code: [GitHub](https://github.com/playground-for-thinker/aurora/tree/main/examples/delhi_air_quality)\n\nThis story map is a JupyterGIS document (`.jGIS`). Open it in notebook.link's JupyterLab view to edit layers and scenes, or rebuild it from pipeline outputs with `build_storymap_jgis.py`.\n",
          "image": "",
          "imageCaption": ""
        },
        "transition": {
